{"name":"Sailing on the Bay","hex":"#aecbd9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sailing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of sail"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Travelling by ship."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sailing"},{"term":"bay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Batuley."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A body of water (especially the sea) contained by a concave shoreline.","A bank or dam to keep back water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sailing","blocks":[{"text":"Sailing employs the wind—acting on sails, wing sails or kites—to propel a craft on the surface of the water, on ice (iceboat) or on land over a chosen course, which is often part of a larger plan of navigation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Regattafeld_vor_Laboe.jpg/330px-Regattafeld_vor_Laboe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sailing","wikidata":"Q192520"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q900906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Tarangini.jpg/500px-Tarangini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Tarangini.jpg/500px-Tarangini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATarangini.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/L-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg/250px-L-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/63/L-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/L-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg/250px-L-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AL-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/DN_ice_boat--Ice_Nine--Lake_Sunapee_NH.jpg/500px-DN_ice_boat--Ice_Nine--Lake_Sunapee_NH.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/DN_ice_boat--Ice_Nine--Lake_Sunapee_NH.jpg/1280px-DN_ice_boat--Ice_Nine--Lake_Sunapee_NH.jpg?utm_source=en.wik